==Hindi==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|sa|hi}} {{term|वस्तु|tr=vastu|lang=sa|sc=Deva}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ʋəst̪u]|lang=hi}}

===Noun===
{{hi-noun|g=f|tr=vastu|ur=وستو}}

# a [[thing]]
# [[stuff]]
# [[baggage]]
# [[material]]
# something real or existent
# a [[commodity]]
# essential [[property]], [[nature]], [[essence]], [[substance]]
# the [[object]] (of); the pith or substance (of)

====Declension====
{{hi-noun-u-uẽ|वस्त|vast}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|hi|चीज़}}

===References===
* McGregor, R.S, ed. ''The Oxford Hindi-English Dictionary'', Oxford university press. 1993
* Platts, John T. ''[http://dsal.uchicago.edu/dictionaries/platts/ A dictionary of Urdu, Classical Hindi, and English]'' Oxford. 1884. [http://dsal.uchicago.edu/cgi-bin/philologic/getobject.pl?c.7:1:4901.platts]

